{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VLQrVBpv2CkdvqZ2K9DiW2","type":"tool_result","content":"r\"\"\"elrule - the FIXED Error List predictor (card 143-3, PD333(b)) as a SHARED module (card chat-S5, PD337(c); moved here\nfrom tools/bench/prep_c143_3_elrule.py, which now re-exports it), plus the BY-DESIGN verdict errorlist_check uses on a\ngood result. OFFLINE, pure (reads JSON states only, no LabVIEW).\n\nThe rule, as SETS of item keys so an item that closes is debited and none is counted twice:\n  L  ('local', node)   a Local whose every terminal row is unwired      -> EL \"Local Variable ...: not connected to anything\"\n  C  ('cond', body)    a While body Diagram's '' SINK row unwired        -> EL \"While Loop: Conditional terminal is not wired\"\n                       (WhileLoop owns no terminal row; its cond terminal is the '' sink row of its body Diagram, 143-2 run 1)\n  SR ('sr', rsr)       a RightShiftRegister whose InnerTerminal SINK row is unwired -> EL \"Shift Register: unwired from inside the\n                       loop\" (bench card 144-a2-2 in arm A13K, measured on the s03 scratch; ported to main by card chat-T5, PD349).\n                       An unwired OuterTerminal (source) of the RSR and the LeftShiftRegister's unwired InnerTerminal (source) give\n                       NO item (measured: 4 such rows, 0 items). Applies to every RSR, created or base.\n  A  ('input', node)   a node in `created` (made by this or an earlier counted session), not an L item, with an unwired sink\n                       (ControlTerminal rows excluded, as PD322(e))  -> EL \"... contains unwired or bad terminal\"\n                       NARROWED by terminal CLASS (PD349): a sink row that is already the C row (a While body Diagram's '' cond\n                       row) or the SR row (an RSR InnerTerminal sink) is not counted again as an A item; the node is A only when\n                       ANOTHER unwired sink remains (measured: the created body #29699 whose only unwired sink is its cond row gave\n                       ONE item, the cond item - the old rule counted it as C AND A, s03 56 vs measured 55 in all four bench arms;\n                       the created RSRs gave only the SR item). No per-uid exception.\n                       SUBVI CALLS (card 145-a2-2, PD351(c)): a created node of owner_class 'SubVI' (the class the simulator\n# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ by design (PD337(c))\nL_RE = re.compile(r\"local\\s*variable.*not\\s*connected|local\\s*or\\s*global\\s*variable\\s*is\\s*not\\s*wired\", re.I | re.S)  # 2nd: empty-raw row, card 145-a2-5\nC_RE = re.compile(r\"while\\s*loop.*conditional\\s*terminal.*not\\s*wired\", re.I | re.S)\nSR_RE = re.compile(r\"shift\\s*register.*unwired\\s*from\\s*inside\", re.I | re.S)\n\n\ndef item_class(text):\n    \"\"\"'local' | 'cond' | 'sr' | None for one Error List item text (raw + detail).\"\"\"\n    t = str(text or \"\")\n    if L_RE.search(t):\n        return \"local\"\n    if C_RE.search(t):\n        return \"cond\"\n    if SR_RE.search(t):\n        return \"sr\"\n    return None\n\n\ndef _j(p):\n    return json.load(open(p if os.path.isabs(p) else os.path.join(ROOT, p), encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n\n325:## GUI error-list reader — `tools/lv_errorlist.py` (2026-09-23, connectivity-map-plan STEP 2)\n329:| **purpose** | the errors of a BROKEN VI, read from LabVIEW's own Error List (Ctrl+L, keyboard; the arrow/Run toolbar is never clicked). `read(vi_path, out_json)` → `{items:[{index,vi,object,reason,raw,detail}], n_reported, gui_acts, …}` → `tools/bench/errorlist_<vi>_<date>.json` |\n330:| **accessibility: NO** | the Error List (`LVDChild`, title `Error list`) is **fully owner-drawn** — **0** win32 child windows, a **7**-element UIA tree holding only title-bar chrome, **1** MSAA object (the window). 0 rows by either route. `tools/bench/errorlist_test.log` |\n336:| 🆕 **`-Action activate`** | **`-Action focus` AND `-Action clickprobe` DISMISS ANY ESC-CLOSING DIALOG**: `[LVGui]::Focus` (`tools/lv_gui.ps1:243`) and `[LVGui]::ClickProbe` (`tools/lv_gui.ps1:372`) both send **VK_ESCAPE** after activating. Measured twice on the Error List — after either call, `rect`/`shotwin` report \"No LabVIEW window whose title contains 'Error list'\". **`-Action activate`** (`[LVGui]::Activate`) is that activation minus the Alt tap and minus the Esc: AttachThreadInput + SetForegroundWindow, returning one JSON line with the measured `fg_after` and `ok`. Same gate, same log. Self-test: `activate` then `rect` on the same title — `ok:true`, window still alive |\n1051:| [`tools/errorlist_check.py`](#tools-errorlist-check-py) | shared module | 87 | 27 | 10 | 0 |\n1073:| [`tools/lv_errorlist.py`](#tools-lv-errorlist-py) | shared module | 5 | 25 | 12 | 0 |\n1280:shared module; imported by 74 file(s): `tools/bench/allterms_s4.py`, `tools/bench/allterms_v1_check.py`, `tools/bench/diag_c100_6_maxmin.py`, `tools/bench/diag_c103_wait_donor.py`, `tools/bench/diag_c111_b1_errorlist.py`, `tools/bench/diag_c112b_opuid.py` ...\n1396:| `errorlist_hook` | n, a, bench, runner_log, status_text | User decision 5, 2026-09-24 (\"사이클 시작하기 전에 LabVIEW 컴파일 에러 창은 반드시 확인해야할듯\"): before every | docstring | - | 833 |\n1403:| `write_cycle_card` | bench, n, status_text, model, effort, ff_recipe, motor_verdict, a, errorlist=None, steer=None, note=None, gates=None | C1: '<bench>/cards/cycle_<n>.json', validated against docs/protocol/cycle.json. Returns (path, None) or | docstring | - | 1181 |\n1528:| `item_class` | text | 'local' / 'cond' / 'sr' / None for one Error List item text (raw + detail). | docstring | - | 201 |\n1530:| `by_design_verdict` | extra, missing, measured_total, base_total, plan=None, prediction=None | ('log'/'stop', rule, detail) - see the module docstring. 'extra'/'missing' = item texts from errorlist_check.compare; | docstring | - | 228 |\n1532:### tools/errorlist_check.py\n1534:shared 